=== God’s plan for the heathen
--- God’s Plan for the Heathen [title]
overline: A Major Theme of the Book of Jonah and the Entire Old Testament
heading: God’s Plan for the Heathen
sub: KJV Old Testament

--- The Lesson of Jonah
lead: The heathen are **not a lost cause** and should not be written off as inevitably doomed.
panel: Jonah 1 | A ship full of pagan sailors **feared the LORD exceedingly, offered a sacrifice unto the LORD, and made vows** after seeing His power. [[Jonah 1:16]]
panel: Jonah 3 | The entire city of Nineveh repented on a scale **unparalleled elsewhere in Scripture**. [[Jonah 3:5-10]]
p: The Word of God is powerful. Its ability to change hearts and minds should **never be underestimated**.

--- Every Creature
p: Christians must not pick and choose whom to evangelize. The command is clear: “Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to **every creature**.” [[Mark 16:15]]
p: If we sow the seed, God promises souls will be saved: “He that goeth forth and weepeth, bearing precious seed, shall doubtless come again with rejoicing, bringing his sheaves with him.” [[Psalm 126:6]]

--- God Always Planned to Save the Gentiles
xr: Deuteronomy 4:6-8 | The Mosaic Law said other nations would hear of Israel’s righteous laws and say, “Surely this great nation is a wise and understanding people.”
xr: Exodus 12:48 | The Law allowed foreigners to be circumcised and keep the Passover, becoming full Israelites.
xr: Ezekiel 47:22-23 | This naturalization of strangers is spelled out again in Ezekiel.

--- God Always Planned to Save the Gentiles (continued)
xr: 2 Chronicles 6:32-33 | Solomon prayed that foreigners from far countries would come, pray toward the temple, and know the name of the LORD.
xr: Isaiah 56:7 | God’s house shall be called “a house of prayer for all people.”
xr: Acts 10:35 | Peter confirmed in the New Testament: “In every nation he that feareth him, and worketh righteousness, is accepted with him.”

--- Named Gentile Believers in the KJV Old Testament
kicker: Genesis 12 onward, not descendants of Jacob
group: 1. Melchizedek | King of Salem, priest of the most high God (possibly a pre-incarnate Christ). | Genesis 14:18-20
group: 2. Abimelech, King of Gerar | Acknowledged God was with Abraham & Isaac; made covenants in the name of the LORD. (Genesis 20–21, 26) |
group: 3. Jethro (Reuel) | Midianite priest who confessed, “Now I know that the LORD is greater than all gods.” | Exodus 18:9-12
group: 4. Rahab the Canaanite | “The LORD your God, he is God in heaven above, and in earth beneath.” | Joshua 2:11; Joshua 6:25

--- Named Gentile Believers (continued)
kicker: Genesis 12 onward, not descendants of Jacob
group: 5. The Gibeonites | Canaanites who entered covenant with Israel and served at the tabernacle. (Joshua 9–10) |
group: 6. Ruth the Moabitess | “Thy people shall be my people, and thy God my God.” | Ruth 1:16
group: 7. The Queen of Sheba | Blessed “the LORD thy God” and glorified His name. | 1 Kings 10:1-9; 2 Chronicles 9:1-8
group: 8. Hiram, King of Tyre | Blessed “the LORD God of Israel, that made heaven and earth.” | 2 Chronicles 2:12

--- Named Gentile Believers (continued)
kicker: Genesis 12 onward, not descendants of Jacob
group: 9. Widow of Zarephath | “I know that … the word of the LORD in thy mouth is truth.” | 1 Kings 17:24
group: 10. Naaman the Syrian | “I know that there is no God in all the earth, but in Israel” — vowed to worship only YHWH. | 2 Kings 5:15-17
group: 11. Nebuchadnezzar | “I Nebuchadnezzar praise and extol and honour the King of heaven … whose dominion is an everlasting dominion.” | Daniel 4:34-37; Daniel 2:47; Daniel 3:28-29

--- Named Gentile Believers (continued)
kicker: Genesis 12 onward, not descendants of Jacob
group: 12. Job | Righteous Gentile from Uz who feared God and eschewed evil. (Book of Job) |
group: 13. Cyrus, King of Persia | Called God’s anointed and shepherd; proclaimed the LORD gave him all kingdoms and commanded the temple rebuilt. | 2 Chronicles 36:22-23; Isaiah 44:28; Isaiah 45:1-4

--- Other Notable Mentions
- The heathen sailors who sacrificed to the LORD ([[Jonah 1:14-16]])
- The entire city of Nineveh that repented (Jonah 3)
- Many Persians who “became Jews” for fear of the LORD ([[Esther 8:17]])
take: God is willing that **NONE** should perish. The heathen are NOT beyond the reach of His mercy and the power of His Word!

=== Salvation: A Finished Work
--- Salvation: A Finished Work [title]
overline: Recap
heading: Salvation: A Finished Work
sub: By Grace Through Faith

--- I. The Drawing to Christ
kicker: Distinct Roles in the Godhead
scripture: John 6:44
p: (The Father draws men to Jesus before the crucifixion.)
scripture: John 12:32
p: (Jesus draws all men to Himself after the crucifixion.)

--- I. The Drawing to Christ (continued)
kicker: Distinct Roles in the Godhead
scripture: John 16:8-11
callout: **Note:** The Holy Spirit is never said to “draw” men to Christ; His role is conviction of the world concerning sin (unbelief), righteousness (now in Christ), and judgment (already executed on Satan, unbelievers in the time to come), alongside regeneration and sealing.

--- II. How Faith Comes
kicker: Justification and Imputation of Righteousness
scripture: Romans 10:17
scripture: Romans 4:5-8

--- II. Justification and Imputation of Righteousness
kicker: How Faith Comes, Justification, and Imputation of Righteousness
scripture: Romans 5:1-2
scripture: Romans 5:9
scripture: 2 Corinthians 5:21
p: At the moment of faith, God declares the believer righteous (justification) by imputing Christ’s perfect righteousness to us and our sin to Him. This is the Father’s judicial act based on the Son’s work at the cross.

--- III. The Full Scope of Salvation
kicker: Reconciled by His Death, Saved by His Life
scripture: John 19:30
scripture: Romans 5:10
scripture: Romans 5:11
scripture: Romans 4:25

--- III. Reconciled by His Death, Saved by His Life
kicker: The Full Scope of Salvation
p: The redemptive price and atonement were fully paid and finished at the cross: “It is finished.” Christ still has future acts to do, the rapture/resurrection, the rewards of the faithful, the wrath on the unbelieving, Millennial rule. But reconciliation was finished by His death on the cross.
p: Reconciliation is by His death alone. But the ongoing and ultimate salvation, deliverance from sin’s power, wrath, and presence, is by His resurrection, by His life, the living union with the risen Christ who ever lives.

--- IV. Regeneration, Renewing, and Baptism by the Holy Spirit
kicker: At the Moment of Faith
p: (This is the Spirit’s baptizing us into Christ, placing us into the body of Christ, and the new birth.)
scripture: Titus 3:5
scripture: John 3:5-6

--- IV. Regeneration, Renewing, and Baptism (continued)
kicker: At the Moment of Faith
scripture: 1 Corinthians 12:13
scripture: Ephesians 1:13
p: All this happens the instant we believe: the Holy Spirit regenerates us (new birth), renews us, baptizes us into vital union with the living Christ, and seals us forever as God’s possession as the earnest towards the purchased possession. Electing us to be predestinated to be conformed to His image and glorified, adopted as children and made joint-heirs with Christ to the Kingdom.

--- V. Adoption and the Future Consummation
kicker: The Day of Redemption (Our Blessed Hope)
scripture: Titus 2:13
scripture: Romans 8:23
scripture: Ephesians 1:14

--- V. The Day of Redemption (Our Blessed Hope)
kicker: Adoption and the Future Consummation
scripture: Ephesians 4:30
scripture: 1 Thessalonians 4:16-17
p: The payment was finished at the cross, but the full possession of the purchased inheritance, including the redemption of our body at the rapture, is the blessed hope we eagerly await. This is when the living Christ personally takes His church to Himself.

--- VI. The Cosmic Reconciliation
kicker: Restitution of All Things, and Revelation of Christ’s Kingdom
scripture: Colossians 1:20
scripture: Revelation 11:15

--- VI. Revelation of Christ’s Kingdom
kicker: The Cosmic Reconciliation and Restitution of All Things
scripture: Revelation 12:10
scripture: Philippians 2:10-11
p: The price was paid in full at the cross; the full cosmic reconciliation and open manifestation of Christ’s kingdom, Satan cast down forever, every knee bowing, awaits future enforcement when the living Christ returns in glory to subdue all things.

--- VII. The Three Forms of Sanctification
kicker: Positional Sanctification (Past, completed at salvation)
p: (All believers are set apart unto God, elected unto obedience and service now, and made joint-heirs with Christ to reign in the coming kingdom.)
scripture: 1 Corinthians 6:11
scripture: Hebrews 10:10
scripture: 1 Peter 1:2

--- VII. Practical/Progressive Sanctification
kicker: Present, ongoing growth
scripture: 1 Thessalonians 5:23
scripture: 2 Corinthians 3:18
scripture: Ephesians 2:10

--- VII. Ultimate Sanctification
kicker: Future, complete conformity
scripture: 1 John 3:2
scripture: Philippians 3:21
scripture: Romans 8:17
scripture: 2 Timothy 2:12

--- VIII. Intercession
kicker: The Present High Priestly Ministry of the Living Christ
scripture: Hebrews 7:25
scripture: Romans 8:34
p: The living Christ continually intercedes for us, applying the benefits of the cross until He comes again to fully possess what He has purchased in the reconciliation.

--- Conclusion: Eternal Security
kicker: Reconciled by His Death, Saved by His Life, Awaiting the Blessed Hope
scripture: John 10:28-29
scripture: Romans 8:38-39
scripture: 1 Peter 1:3-5

--- Conclusion: Eternal Security (continued)
kicker: Reconciled by His Death, Saved by His Life, Awaiting the Blessed Hope
p: The payment and legal basis were perfectly finished at the cross (“It is finished”), reconciling all of creation to God, giving us access to His grace the moment we believe. But the Scripture plainly teaches the “much more” salvation, eternal life, deliverance, and final redemption, is by the life of the risen Christ who ever lives. We have eternal life now because He lives, we are kept by His life now, that we shall be openly glorified when He appears: that blessed hope wherein the full victory purchased at the cross is manifested for all to see, raised up incorruptible, and we reign with Him as joint-heirs forever.
